      "reason": "The version is read from the graph record graphify_version without running the program, unknown when there is no graph, and update and doctor report the installed version."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-09T16:27:34Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R2-F1",
      "reason": "The manifest and build state are now untrusted input with caps, strict parsing, key validation and an unreadable state; no field is used to open a path."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-09T16:27:34Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R2-F2",
      "reason": "A graph holding non-structural nodes is foreign: queries refuse it and update refuses to write over it, so the module never mixes in or deletes a layer it does not maintain."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-09T16:27:34Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R2-F3",
      "reason": "Every command that starts the program first runs it with the version flag and refuses below the floor, unparseable, or silent; status reads the graph version and warns."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-09T16:29:37Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R3-F1",
      "reason": "The foreign check covers nodes and edges by origin, with a test for a non-structural edge among structural nodes."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-09T16:29:38Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R3-F2",
      "reason": "The helper no longer reproduces the program ignore rules: one conservative walker takes an inventory at update and at status and compares the two, with a cross-check against the manifest, so a difference in ignore semantics cannot hide a new file or keep a graph stale."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-09T16:32:54Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R4-F1",
      "reason": "Every invocation of the program is captured with separate stdout and stderr caps, a time limit, process group kill and a one-line failure state, with tests for oversized output."
    },
